  "verdict": "Gate readings move apart with n: the margin a good arm needs grows with n when every coupon must pass, shrinks under the lower confidence bound (pooled: shrinks) and shrinks under the arm mean — so n and the reading of «≥ threshold» are one decision. Under the arm-mean reading an arm sitting exactly at its threshold passes half the time at every n. Gate E's threshold is full recovery itself, so an electrode recovering exactly 100 % passes with probability 0.5 (arm mean), 0.05 (lower bound) or 0.25…0.015625 (every coupon) — whatever the spread. At the coupon letter's quote point (12 per alloy, 19 for Ti-6Al-4V) the two-arm alloys Ta, Ti-13Nb-13Zr, Ti-15Zr, Ti-6Al-7Nb carry their electrode coupons as 2 + 1, i.e. one arm on a single replicate; the gold coupon is single by order."
